5|0@sysadmin^1438698978#ctr4036:Kynaeus$:As others have said, this is not your problem to deal with other than imaging them a new device. Suggest to the bosses set up a process to charge back to the damaging users' departmental budget, when they see there is a cost to replacing $2k business laptops, and that cost is $8k for one quarter + manpower hours, it won't take long for the capex's to pile up and change their minds about being lax on such people
2|0@sysadmin^1438699084#ctr42at:rev0lutn$:I agree with what has been said already about it being a Business Management / H.R. issue not an I.T. one, however there is of course the reality we face of the user still breaking stuff (repeatedly). We had one particularly damage prone user awhile back and we made the business purchase a special unit eventually. SSD not a HDD and comprehensive warranty that covered even physical damage, whereas our typical warranty is only for hardware failure, not abuse. But we are an all Dell shop, so may not be possible in your case. 
