10|0@sysadmin^1438696935#ctr2vdp:sirdudethefirst$:Talk to his boss. Make sure your boss is there. Make sure HR is there. A long time ago I had a user who kept complaining that their dialup modem (this is how long ago this was) would not work unless they dropped the laptop from 6" off the table. This was the 3rd laptop in a year he complained about. After taking the laptop apart I noticed that the board was cracked. I documented it and took a picture of it (2megapixel camera ftw) then my boss and I went to his boss with it. After a bit of back and forth I got him to admit that his dog loved pulling on cables and every laptop he had would at one point or another be pulled from its cable and fall on the floor from 3-4 feet height. He did dare to claim that laptops should survive such a drop to which I said, "well let's take into account the height of the drop and the weight of the laptop. Now let's do some math and find out if you can survive a corresponding drop." He stopped talking and secured his cables better on the table. My boss at the time was a bit uncomfortable :) I was young and had a big mouth. Now I just have a big mouth.
